# SonarQube for IDE (code quality)

Analyze only `app/frontend/src` and `app/backend/app`. Do not create `frontend/` or `backend/` at the repository root — leftover Problems on those paths are stale.

When editing a file:

- Fix Blocker and Critical issues in that file before moving on
- Do not hardcode passwords, API keys, or JWT secrets
- Prefer early returns over deep nesting (cognitive complexity)
- Date regexes must use `[0-9]`, not `\\d` (Python `\\d` matches Thai digits)
- Do not use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` for extracted or user TOR text
